turned when several exist is not specified, but the same input always"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"gives the same cut. When the edges of positive capacity do not connect the graph, the cut"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of value zero whose source side is the first vertex’s component, with every crossing edge"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(all of capacity zero). Parallel capacities add; self-loops are ignored. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"capacity"},{"type":"text","text":" is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"called once per non-loop edge, in position order, before any work (self-loops are never"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"asked). O(nm log n) in the worst case, far less when contractions are many."}],"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Flows\/documentation\/Flows\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/minimumCut(capacity:)","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"references":{"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/DirectedView":{"url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/directedview","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An undirected graph read as a directed graph: each edge "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"{u, v}"},{"type":"text","text":" is the two arcs "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"u→v"},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"v→u","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", so "},{"code":"successors","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"predecessors","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" are both "},{"code":"neighbors","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"code":"edgeCount","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is twice the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"base’s."}],"type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"DirectedView"}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"DirectedV